bdwgc in gocpp
==============

This folder is the vendored source of the Boehm-Demers-Weiser conservative
garbage collector (bdwgc), the collector of gocpp's GC engine (phase 16
README section 2.4). It is embedded in the gocpp binary (runtime/bdwgc.go,
package rtfiles) and built by internal/build (internal/build/bdwgc.go) into
the object/archive cache, once per C compiler, compiler version, sanitizer,
target and flag set. Nothing links it unless a program asks for it.

Upstream
--------
  URL:    https://github.com/bdwgc/bdwgc
  tag:    v8.2.12
  commit: 4fab5386df64466b2b61fc7209bef033cad1e6cc
  release: 2026-02-05
  archive: https://github.com/bdwgc/bdwgc/archive/refs/tags/v8.2.12.tar.gz
  sha256: d09001f45dabf1c29a5df3e63020a4bab5ad4aad69137bb07100c717e2ecba0b
  vendored: 2026-10-24

The upstream release has no LICENSE file. LICENSE is the "Copyright &
Warranty" section of README.md, reproduced verbatim (README.md itself is
upstream's, unchanged).

What is here
------------
  src/       the C sources of the Linux build (27 files; the list is the one
             of bdwgc's CMakeLists.txt for Linux with threads, parallel
             marking, thread-local allocation, gcj support and the disclaim
             interface), and src/windows/win32_threads.c, the Windows thread
             layer (byte-identical upstream). The MinGW build itself (its
             defines, OS layer and link flags) is M10 work; rtfiles.BdwgcSources
             already returns its source list for "windows" (23 files, the CMake
             Win32-threads branch). M10 must record the thread backend: MinGW-w64
             and llvm-mingw ship winpthreads, so a CMake configure would take the
             CMAKE_USE_PTHREADS_INIT + WIN32 branch and add gc_dlopen.c and
             specific.c (25 files). Both files are vendored, so the tree is
             complete for either backend.
  include/   the public and private headers (upstream's include/, without
             include/include.am and include/extra/)
  LICENSE    see above
  README.md  upstream's README, unchanged
  VERSION    gocpp's file (upstream has none): the version of the tree

What was pruned
---------------
Everything outside the collector's C library:
  - the build systems (CMakeLists.txt, configure.ac, Makefile.am, the MSVC,
    Watcom, OS/2 and Amiga makefiles, autogen.sh, m4/, build/);
  - the tests (tests/), the documentation (doc/), the C++ interface and cord
    libraries (gc_cpp.cc, gc_cpp.cpp, gc_badalc.cc, gc_badalc.cpp, cord/,
    tools/), and the top-level extra/ (extra/gc.c, the single-object build, and
    extra/msvc_dbg.c, MSVC only);
  - the platform sources that neither build compiles (darwin_stop_world.c, the
    ia64 and sparc assembly);
  - include/include.am (build metadata) and include/extra/ (the deprecated
    wrapper headers).
Nothing that either build compiles or includes is missing; a file whose name
starts with "." or "_" would be skipped by //go:embed, and the tree has none
(runtime/bdwgc_test.go checks it).

Configuration
-------------
bdwgc is configured with -D flags, not with configure or CMake (no config.h:
HAVE_CONFIG_H is not defined). The fixed defines of phase 16 section 2.4 are
GC_THREADS, PARALLEL_MARK, THREAD_LOCAL_ALLOC, GC_BUILTIN_ATOMIC,
LARGE_CONFIG, USE_MMAP, USE_MUNMAP, ALL_INTERIOR_POINTERS and
GC_DISABLE_INCREMENTAL (gocpp's runtime owns SIGSEGV; the write-fault handler
of MPROTECT_VDB/SOFT_VDB must not exist, and GC_enable_incremental is a
no-op), and DONT_ADD_BYTE_AT_END is not defined. The build adds what bdwgc's
own CMakeLists.txt adds on Linux: NO_EXECUTE_PERMISSION, _REENTRANT,
GC_GCJ_SUPPORT, GC_ENABLE_SUSPEND_THREAD, ENABLE_DISCLAIM,
JAVA_FINALIZATION, GC_ATOMIC_UNCOLLECTABLE, HANDLE_FORK, the platform probes
HAVE_DL_ITERATE_PHDR, HAVE_DLADDR and HAVE_PTHREAD_SETNAME_NP_WITH_TID, and
GC_NO_THREAD_REDIRECTS (phase 16 section 2.5: registration is explicit, so
gc.h must not turn pthread_create into GC_pthread_create). See bdwgcDefines
in internal/build/bdwgc.go for the exact list; it is part of the cache key.

Update procedure
----------------
1. Download https://github.com/bdwgc/bdwgc/archive/refs/tags/vX.Y.Z.tar.gz,
   check the tag's commit with the GitHub API, and record the archive's
   sha256.
2. Replace src/ and include/ from the new tree, with the same pruning (check
   the source list against the new CMakeLists.txt: a new source file must be
   added, and a removed one taken out).
3. Update VERSION and this file (URL, tag, commit, release date, sha256,
   date, and what changed).
4. Run `go test ./runtime -run 'TestBdwgc'` and the focused tests of
   internal/build; the smoke test (runtime/test/bdwgc_test.cpp) must print
   OK with g++ and clang++, at -O0 and -O2, and under ASan and TSan.
